---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  tittel="Terms and disclaimer"
  beskrivelse="Terms of use for The Dream Guide. What the content is meant to be, what it is not, and what responsibility we take for the information on this site."
>
  <div class="static-page">
    <span class="static-label">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="static-title">Terms and disclaimer</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        The Dream Guide is an editorial site about dreams, symbols and sleep.
        The content is meant as information and reflection — not as medical,
        psychological or health advice. This page explains what you can and
        cannot expect from us.
      </p>

      <p><em>Last updated: 24 August 2026</em></p>

      <h2>Who is behind this site</h2>
      <p>
        The Dream Guide is the English edition of drommeguiden.no, owned and
        operated by Herman Gautefall Olsson in Norway. The content is edited by
        The Dream Guide's editorial team. You can read more about how we work on
        <a href="/en/about/">About us</a>, and reach us through the
        <a href="/en/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>This is not health advice</h2>
      <p>
        We are not psychologists, psychiatrists, therapists or doctors, and we
        do not present ourselves as such. Nothing on The Dream Guide is a
        diagnosis, a treatment or a recommendation for treatment, and the
        content is not a substitute for contact with a qualified health
        professional.
      </p>
      <p>
        This applies in particular to the sleep section. Although the articles
        draw on published research and public health sources, they are general
        accounts — not advice tailored to your situation. If you have persistent
        sleep problems, nightmares that distress you, or mental health
        difficulties, please contact your doctor, a sleep clinic or another
        qualified health service.
      </p>
      <p>
        In an acute crisis, contact your local emergency number — <strong>112</strong>
        across the EU and EEA, <strong>911</strong> in the United States,
        <strong>999</strong> in the United Kingdom. Free crisis lines are
        available in most countries, including <strong>988</strong> in the
        United States and <strong>116 123</strong> in the United Kingdom and
        much of Europe.
      </p>

      <h2>About dream interpretation</h2>
      <p>
        Dream interpretation is not an exact science, and we do not pretend that
        it is. Our symbol pages describe how a motif has been understood across
        different traditions and fields — from classical dream literature to
        modern dream research. We deliberately write "may mean" and "is often
        read as", never "means".
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not claim that dreams predict the future, reveal truths about
        other people, or give answers that hold regardless of who you are. The
        interpretation is always your own. Do not make important decisions about
        health, money or relationships on the basis of a dream interpretation.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and updates</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep the content accurate and current, but cannot guarantee
        that everything is complete, error-free or in line with the latest
        research at all times. Knowledge changes, particularly in sleep science.
        If you find an error, an outdated claim or something imprecise, we would
        genuinely appreciate hearing from you through the
        <a href="/en/contact/">contact page</a> — we will correct it.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        You use The Dream Guide at your own risk. We are not liable for loss or
        damage arising from acting on information found on the site, so far as
        the law permits. The site is provided "as is", without guarantees of
        availability or uninterrupted operation.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        We link to external sources when we believe they add value — research
        articles and public health sources, for example. We have no control over
        the content of those sites and take no responsibility for it. A link is
        not an endorsement of everything the publisher offers.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site is funded by advertising, including Google AdSense. Ads are
        labelled as ads and are selected by the ad network, not by us
        editorially. An ad appearing on a page does not mean we recommend the
        product or service. Editorial content and advertising are kept separate
        — we do not write articles in order to sell anything.
      </p>
      <p>
        How cookies are used in connection with advertising is described in the
        <a href="/en/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and on the
        <a href="/en/cookies/">cookie page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Copyright</h2>
      <p>
        The texts on The Dream Guide are our own editorial work and are
        protected by copyright. You are welcome to quote briefly from us with a
        clear attribution and a link, but not to copy whole articles or publish
        our content as your own.
      </p>
      <p>
        Photographs are sourced from Pexels and used in accordance with their
        licence. The photographer is credited on the pages where the image
        appears.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the site changes. The date at the top shows
        when they were last revised. Continued use of the site after a change
        counts as acceptance of the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        The site is operated from Norway, and these terms are governed by
        Norwegian law. If you are a consumer, this does not affect any rights
        you have under the mandatory consumer law of your country of residence.
        Any dispute will first be pursued amicably.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .static-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 8px 0 40px;
  }
  .static-label {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-nav);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .static-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 40px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-text-heading);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .static-title { font-size: 52px; }
  }
  .prose .lead {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
</style>
